{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0198sL2eGZx3ktLSnpVTAgxH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EtHMBTqbcJGhJSFRoWaLBg","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"Implementer","description":"Implement sos_1","prompt":"You are the Implementer agent. Your job is to make ALL tests pass for card sos_1 by implementing the card and making any necessary engine changes.\n\n## Card\n- Card ID: sos_1\n- Spec path: cards/sos/sos_1/card_spec.json\n- Implementation file: cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\n- Test file to satisfy: cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py (DO NOT MODIFY THIS FILE)\n\n## Test files (must not be modified)\nRead /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-files.txt for the list of test files. You MUST NOT modify any of these files.\n\n## Reference materials\n- Read AGENTS.md and PROJECT_MAP.md for workspace rules.\n- Read cards/sos/sos_1/card_spec.json for the card specification.\n- Read cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py to understand what the tests expect.\n- Look at FDN reference implementations: cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py (read several to understand patterns).\n- Read engine source: engine/card.py, engine/events.py, engine/triggers.py, engine/replacement_effects.py, engine/zones.py, engine/types.py\n- Grep RULEBOOK.txt for relevant rules about the card's mechanics.\n- Read KEY_DECISIONS.md for any prior conventions.\n- Read FILES_MODIFIED.json for files already changed by other cards.\n\n## Instructions\n1. Read the test file to understand exactly what's expected.\n2. Read the card spec and engine source to understand the API.\n3. Implement the card in cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py.\n4. You may also modify engine files (add methods, extend existing functions) if needed to support the card's mechanics. Do NOT rename or delete existing engine code.\n5. Run the tests with `python -m pytest cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py -x -v` to verify they pass.\n6. Also run `python -m pytest engine_tests/ -x -v` to ensure no engine regressions.\n7. Also run `python -m pytest cards/fdn/ -x -v` to ensure no FDN regressions.\n\n## Output\n- Write a diff to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl.diff using `git diff`\n- Write a rationale to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md explaining your implementation approach.\n- Write a file list to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-files.txt listing all files you modified (one per line).\n- Update FILES_MODIFIED.json at the repo root — upsert an entry for card sos_1 with shape: {\"card\": \"sos_1\", \"tests\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}], \"implementation\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}]}\n\n## Return format\nReturn a short status summary:\n```\nIMPL_DONE (or DISPUTE)\nfiles_changed: N\ntests_passing: all (or list failing)\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: one-line summary\n```\n\nIf a test is genuinely wrong (tests something impossible in the engine), return DISPUTE with disputed_tests list and write /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-dispute.md explaining why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152,"cache_read_input_tokens":17672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":152},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"12b03d76-73c6-4f8b-a3fa-692a65d4355e","request_id":"req_011CbUqKxJz2deRc8uz3caRE"}
