{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012HHsi7cuHJh8NfvCHzVQf4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale for SOS 1 -- The Dawning Archaic\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Card Class Structure\n6\t- Extends `Creature` (as required by spec: 7/7 Legendary Creature - Avatar).\n7\t- Uses `kwargs.setdefault()` pattern consistent with all FDN reference implementations.\n8\t- Sets `Supertype.LEGENDARY` (enum) rather than a string, matching engine conventions.\n9\t\n10\t### Cost Reduction\n11\t- Implemented `cost_reduction(game)` that counts instants and sorceries in the controller's graveyard.\n12\t- Returns the raw count (not clamped), consistent with test expectations -- the engine's `get_cost_reduction()` handles clamping at generic cost.\n13\t- Uses `self.controller` (the caster) to determine \"your graveyard\", falling back to `self.owner`.\n14\t\n15\t### Attack Trigger\n16\t- Registered via `register_triggers()` using `TriggerRegistration` with `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n17\t- Condition function checks `event.creature is source` to ensure only self-attacks trigger.\n18\t- Effect function:\n19\t  1. Finds valid targets (instant/sorcery cards in controller's graveyard).\n20\t  2. Lets player choose a target via `ctrl.choose()`.\n21\t  3. Validates the chosen card is actually an instant/sorcery (rejects creatures).\n22\t  4. Asks \"you may cast\" via `ctrl.choose_yes_no()`.\n23\t  5. Uses `cast_spell_free()` to cast from graveyard without paying mana cost.\n24\t\n25\t### Exile Replacement Effect\n26\t- Uses a marker attribute `_dawning_archaic_exile` on the card being cast.\n27\t- Modified `_resolve_spell()` in `engine/casting.py` to check for this marker: if present, the instant/sorcery goes to exile instead of graveyard upon resolution.\n28\t- This is an additive body modification to the existing function, which is allowed.\n29\t- The marker is cleaned up after use (deleted from the card object).\n30\t\n31\t### Why a marker flag instead of ReplacementManager\n32\t- The engine's `ReplacementManager` is designed for battlefield-leaving replacement effects (`MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`). Stack-to-graveyard transitions (spell resolution) don't go through the replacement system.\n33\t- Adding a full replacement event for stack-to-graveyard would require deeper engine restructuring.\n34\t- The marker pattern is simple, reliable, and scoped to this specific card interaction.\n35\t\n36\t## Conventions Established\n37\t- For cards that exile spells cast from graveyard (\"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"), a `_<source>_exile` marker attribute on the card is checked in `_resolve_spell()`.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"318f7cb6-7d06-43fc-8e24-8152634d5750","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:53:26.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale for SOS 1 -- The Dawning Archaic\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Card Class Structure\n- Extends `Creature` (as required by spec: 7/7 Legendary Creature - Avatar).\n- Uses `kwargs.setdefault()` pattern consistent with all FDN reference implementations.\n- Sets `Supertype.LEGENDARY` (enum) rather than a string, matching engine conventions.\n\n### Cost Reduction\n- Implemented `cost_reduction(game)` that counts instants and sorceries in the controller's graveyard.\n- Returns the raw count (not clamped), consistent with test expectations -- the engine's `get_cost_reduction()` handles clamping at generic cost.\n- Uses `self.controller` (the caster) to determine \"your graveyard\", falling back to `self.owner`.\n\n### Attack Trigger\n- Registered via `register_triggers()` using `TriggerRegistration` with `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n- Condition function checks `event.creature is source` to ensure only self-attacks trigger.\n- Effect function:\n  1. Finds valid targets (instant/sorcery cards in controller's graveyard).\n  2. Lets player choose a target via `ctrl.choose()`.\n  3. Validates the chosen card is actually an instant/sorcery (rejects creatures).\n  4. Asks \"you may cast\" via `ctrl.choose_yes_no()`.\n  5. Uses `cast_spell_free()` to cast from graveyard without paying mana cost.\n\n### Exile Replacement Effect\n- Uses a marker attribute `_dawning_archaic_exile` on the card being cast.\n- Modified `_resolve_spell()` in `engine/casting.py` to check for this marker: if present, the instant/sorcery goes to exile instead of graveyard upon resolution.\n- This is an additive body modification to the existing function, which is allowed.\n- The marker is cleaned up after use (deleted from the card object).\n\n### Why a marker flag instead of ReplacementManager\n- The engine's `ReplacementManager` is designed for battlefield-leaving replacement effects (`MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`). Stack-to-graveyard transitions (spell resolution) don't go through the replacement system.\n- Adding a full replacement event for stack-to-graveyard would require deeper engine restructuring.\n- The marker pattern is simple, reliable, and scoped to this specific card interaction.\n\n## Conventions Established\n- For cards that exile spells cast from graveyard (\"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"), a `_<source>_exile` marker attribute on the card is checked in `_resolve_spell()`.\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
