{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SBGxxShe5zGNomN2Ugh43M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019kpYP63c57ZgQkr11TAtaZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale for SOS 4 — Together as One\n\n## File: cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py\n\nTogether as One is a {6} Sorcery with Converge: \"Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneProperties (4 tests)\nValidates static card data matches the spec:\n- `test_is_sorcery` — card is an instance of Sorcery\n- `test_has_sorcery_card_type` — CardType.SORCERY is in card_types\n- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\"\n- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost is {6} (generic 6)\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting (4 tests)\nValidates that get_targets returns two TargetRequirements:\n- `test_get_targets_returns_two_requirements` — the spell has two targeting requirements (one for the player who draws, one for the damage target)\n- `test_first_target_is_a_player` — first target requirement accepts players (for draw)\n- `test_second_target_accepts_player` — second target (any target) accepts players\n- `test_second_target_accepts_creature` — second target (any target) accepts creatures\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeZeroColors (3 tests)\nValidates X=0 behavior (all colorless mana):\n- `test_zero_colors_no_cards_drawn` — no cards are drawn when X=0\n- `test_zero_colors_no_damage` — no damage dealt when X=0\n- `test_zero_colors_no_life_gain` — no life gained when X=0\n\nThese pass trivially against the stub (which does nothing), but must remain correct after implementation.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeResolve (9 tests)\nTests all three effects at 1, 3, and 5 color values:\n- `test_one_color_draws_one_card` / `test_three_colors_draws_three_cards` / `test_five_colors_draws_five_cards` — target player draws X cards\n- `test_one_color_deals_one_damage` / `test_three_colors_deals_three_damage` / `test_five_colors_deals_five_damage` — X damage to damage target\n- `test_one_color_gains_one_life` / `test_three_colors_gains_three_life` / `test_five_colors_gains_five_life` — controller gains X life\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneEdgeCases (5 tests)\nEdge cases:\n- `test_damage_to_creature` — verifies damage can be dealt to a creature (the \"any target\" clause), checking damage_marked\n- `test_opponent_draws_cards` — target player can be the opponent, who draws the cards\n- `test_controller_gains_life_not_target_player` — \"you\" means the controller, not the target player\n- `test_no_targets_is_noop` — if chosen_targets is not set, resolution should not crash\n- `test_all_three_effects_happen_together` — all three effects (draw, damage, life gain) happen in one resolution\n\n### Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n- **Full casting integration with mana payment**: The casting pipeline already handles colors_spent tracking (tested in engine_tests/test_mana.py and the FDN 205 reference). Testing it end-to-end with cast_spell would require scripting target choices for both target requirements, which is fragile. Instead, we test the on_resolve behavior directly by setting colors_spent, following the pattern from FDN 205's tests.\n- **Countering the spell**: Counterspell interaction is engine-level behavior, not card-specific.\n- **Protection from the spell**: Protection preventing damage is engine-level behavior tested elsewhere.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":67141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rs