{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KCgAoCQCGGdfac2NaFdKfp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale for SOS 4 — Together as One\n2\t\n3\t## File: cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py\n4\t\n5\tTogether as One is a {6} Sorcery with Converge: \"Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n6\t\n7\t### TestTogetherAsOneProperties (4 tests)\n8\tValidates static card data matches the spec:\n9\t- `test_is_sorcery` — card is an instance of Sorcery\n10\t- `test_has_sorcery_card_type` — CardType.SORCERY is in card_types\n11\t- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\"\n12\t- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost is {6} (generic 6)\n13\t\n14\t### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting (4 tests)\n15\tValidates that get_targets returns two TargetRequirements:\n16\t- `test_get_targets_returns_two_requirements` — the spell has two targeting requirements (one for the player who draws, one for the damage target)\n17\t- `test_first_target_is_a_player` — first target requirement accepts players (for draw)\n18\t- `test_second_target_accepts_player` — second target (any target) accepts players\n19\t- `test_second_target_accepts_creature` — second target (any target) accepts creatures\n20\t\n21\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeZeroColors (3 tests)\n22\tValidates X=0 behavior (all colorless mana):\n23\t- `test_zero_colors_no_cards_drawn` — no cards are drawn when X=0\n24\t- `test_zero_colors_no_damage` — no damage dealt when X=0\n25\t- `test_zero_colors_no_life_gain` — no life gained when X=0\n26\t\n27\tThese pass trivially against the stub (which does nothing), but must remain correct after implementation.\n28\t\n29\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeResolve (9 tests)\n30\tTests all three effects at 1, 3, and 5 color values:\n31\t- `test_one_color_draws_one_card` / `test_three_colors_draws_three_cards` / `test_five_colors_draws_five_cards` — target player draws X cards\n32\t- `test_one_color_deals_one_damage` / `test_three_colors_deals_three_damage` / `test_five_colors_deals_five_damage` — X damage to damage target\n33\t- `test_one_color_gains_one_life` / `test_three_colors_gains_three_life` / `test_five_colors_gains_five_life` — controller gains X life\n34\t\n35\t### TestTogetherAsOneEdgeCases (5 tests)\n36\tEdge cases:\n37\t- `test_damage_to_creature` — verifies damage can be dealt to a creature (the \"any target\" clause), checking damage_marked\n38\t- `test_opponent_draws_cards` — target player can be the opponent, who draws the cards\n39\t- `test_controller_gains_life_not_target_player` — \"you\" means the controller, not the target player\n40\t- `test_no_targets_is_noop` — if chosen_targets is not set, resolution should not crash\n41\t- `test_all_three_effects_happen_together` — all three effects (draw, damage, life gain) happen in one resolution\n42\t\n43\t### Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n44\t- **Full casting integration with mana payment**: The casting pipeline already handles colors_spent tracking (tested in engine_tests/test_mana.py and the FDN 205 reference). Testing it end-to-end with cast_spell would require scripting target choices for both target requirements, which is fragile. Instead, we test the on_resolve behavior directly by setting colors_spent, following the pattern from FDN 205's tests.\n45\t- **Countering the spell**: Counterspell interaction is engine-level behavior, not card-specific.\n46\t- **Protection from the spell**: Protection preventing damage is engine-level behavior tested elsewhere.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xw4v2PEk1CZWGgRZgwJJnc","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"c8ea6c78-5505-4a80-9ad5-4e6bdccbf818","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:58:46.037Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_4"}
