{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QTgXS8iMrTYRScBNMhbaDy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_4 (Together as One)\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t- **Sorcery subclass**: Extended `Sorcery` base class which automatically adds `CardType.SORCERY` to `card_types`.\n6\t- **`colors_spent` attribute**: Initialized as an empty list in `__init__`. Tests set this directly (e.g. `card.colors_spent = [Color.WHITE, Color.BLUE]`). X is computed as `len(set(colors_spent))` to count distinct colors.\n7\t- **Targeting**: Returns two `TargetRequirement` objects:\n8\t  1. First targets a player (filter checks for `life` attribute without `card_types`).\n9\t  2. Second targets \"any target\" (player or creature — checks for `life` or `CardType.CREATURE`).\n10\t- **Resolution**: Uses `chosen_targets[0]` for card draw target and `chosen_targets[1]` for damage target. Controller gains life regardless of targets.\n11\t- **Engine helpers used**: `engine.game.draw_card` for card draw, `engine.game.deal_damage` for damage, direct `controller.life += x` for life gain (no dedicated engine helper exists for life gain).\n12\t- **Edge case handling**: Returns early when X=0 or when `chosen_targets` is missing/insufficient, preventing crashes.\n13\t\n14\t## No Engine Modifications\n15\t\n16\tThis card was implemented entirely within `card_impl.py` using existing engine APIs. No engine changes were needed.\n17\t\n18\t## Conventions\n19\t\n20\t- Converge cards can use a `colors_spent` list attribute on the card object, with X = number of distinct colors in the list. This is set by the casting system or directly by tests.\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"697a04e1-5450-4c23-a789-ea8b4da650ad","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:02:08.064Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: sos_4 (Together as One)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n- **Sorcery subclass**: Extended `Sorcery` base class which automatically adds `CardType.SORCERY` to `card_types`.\n- **`colors_spent` attribute**: Initialized as an empty list in `__init__`. Tests set this directly (e.g. `card.colors_spent = [Color.WHITE, Color.BLUE]`). X is computed as `len(set(colors_spent))` to count distinct colors.\n- **Targeting**: Returns two `TargetRequirement` objects:\n  1. First targets a player (filter checks for `life` attribute without `card_types`).\n  2. Second targets \"any target\" (player or creature — checks for `life` or `CardType.CREATURE`).\n- **Resolution**: Uses `chosen_targets[0]` for card draw target and `chosen_targets[1]` for damage target. Controller gains life regardless of targets.\n- **Engine helpers used**: `engine.game.draw_card` for card draw, `engine.game.deal_damage` for damage, direct `controller.life += x` for life gain (no dedicated engine helper exists for life gain).\n- **Edge case handling**: Returns early when X=0 or when `chosen_targets` is missing/insufficient, preventing crashes.\n\n## No Engine Modifications\n\nThis card was implemented entirely within `card_impl.py` using existing engine APIs. No engine changes were needed.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Converge cards can use a `colors_spent` list attribute on the card object, with X = number of distinct colors in the list. This is set by the casting system or directly by tests.\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
