{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NynEfbtT7FNhD5FVtcPe6X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MaHvhpbrBLHfp73YsJYjDW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Creature base class with Creature subtypes\nThe card is a Creature — Cat Cleric with 3/3 stats. Extended the `Creature` class with `subtypes={\"Cat\", \"Cleric\"}`, `base_power=3`, `base_toughness=3`.\n\n### ETB effect via dual mechanism (on_resolve + register_triggers)\nThe engine's `move_to_zone` fires the ETB event **before** registering the card's own triggers. This is by design to prevent self-referencing ETB triggers from retroactively firing. This means a registered self-ETB trigger won't fire on the initial entry.\n\nTo handle both:\n1. **`on_resolve`** pushes a StackObject that executes the ETB effect after the creature has entered the battlefield (for the cast-and-resolve integration path).\n2. **`register_triggers`** registers the ETB trigger for re-entry scenarios (flicker/blink) and to satisfy tests that inspect trigger registration.\n\nBoth delegate to the shared `_do_etb_effect()` function.\n\n### Inkling token creation\nCreates a 1/1 Creature token with `name=\"Inkling\"`, `subtypes={\"Inkling\"}`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING`, `is_token=True`. Uses `engine.game.create_token()` which handles battlefield placement and ETB event firing.\n\n### Prepared designation\nTracked via `self.is_prepared: bool = False` attribute on the card. After token creation, counts creatures on the controller's battlefield vs. each opponent. If any opponent has strictly more creatures, sets `is_prepared = True`.\n\n### Target requirement\nThe `get_targets` method returns a `TargetRequirement` that accepts any player object (detected via `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`).\n\n## Conventions Established\n- Self-ETB effects on creatures should use `on_resolve` to push a StackObject for the initial cast, plus `register_triggers` for re-entry scenarios. Both should delegate to a shared effect function.\n- The `is_prepared` attribute tracks the prepared designation on creatures.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_read_input_tokens":84820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":157,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H6edwdD9h9cdEHviTEV25h","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"12a57a50-86b0-4b08-b72b-6e77b4d0b6d9","request_id":"req_011CbUsCTuUtMcox5Jsui49G","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
