{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UMGdVY4AAhKssyCaL2To8P","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Creature base class with Creature subtypes\n6\tThe card is a Creature — Cat Cleric with 3/3 stats. Extended the `Creature` class with `subtypes={\"Cat\", \"Cleric\"}`, `base_power=3`, `base_toughness=3`.\n7\t\n8\t### ETB effect via dual mechanism (on_resolve + register_triggers)\n9\tThe engine's `move_to_zone` fires the ETB event **before** registering the card's own triggers. This is by design to prevent self-referencing ETB triggers from retroactively firing. This means a registered self-ETB trigger won't fire on the initial entry.\n10\t\n11\tTo handle both:\n12\t1. **`on_resolve`** pushes a StackObject that executes the ETB effect after the creature has entered the battlefield (for the cast-and-resolve integration path).\n13\t2. **`register_triggers`** registers the ETB trigger for re-entry scenarios (flicker/blink) and to satisfy tests that inspect trigger registration.\n14\t\n15\tBoth delegate to the shared `_do_etb_effect()` function.\n16\t\n17\t### Inkling token creation\n18\tCreates a 1/1 Creature token with `name=\"Inkling\"`, `subtypes={\"Inkling\"}`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING`, `is_token=True`. Uses `engine.game.create_token()` which handles battlefield placement and ETB event firing.\n19\t\n20\t### Prepared designation\n21\tTracked via `self.is_prepared: bool = False` attribute on the card. After token creation, counts creatures on the controller's battlefield vs. each opponent. If any opponent has strictly more creatures, sets `is_prepared = True`.\n22\t\n23\t### Target requirement\n24\tThe `get_targets` method returns a `TargetRequirement` that accepts any player object (detected via `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`).\n25\t\n26\t## Conventions Established\n27\t- Self-ETB effects on creatures should use `on_resolve` to push a StackObject for the initial cast, plus `register_triggers` for re-entry scenarios. Both should delegate to a shared effect function.\n28\t- The `is_prepared` attribute tracks the prepared designation on creatures.\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ChGr58yCcpZRkviDx6c1ub","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"fe758cfd-2a3e-4e49-8dc6-b4224b4678f5","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:13:40.034Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_13 prepared mechanic"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016j3CXEwuxP3kQAeviJxRsG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tdiff --git a/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py b/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\n2\tindex 765fb45..9c6ef88 100644\n3\t--- a/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\n4\t+++ b/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py\n5\t@@ -2,15 +2,159 @@\n6\t \n7\t from __future__ import annotations\n8\t \n9\t-from engine.card import CardImpl\n10\t+from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n11\t \n12\t-from typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n13\t+from engine.card import Creature\n14\t+from engine.events import EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent\n15\t+from engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, TargetRequirement, Zone\n16\t \n17\t if TYPE_CHECKING:\n18\t     from engine.game_state import GameState\n19\t \n20\t \n21\t-class EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(CardImpl):\n22\t-    \"\"\"TODO: Implement Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares.\"\"\"\n23\t+class EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature):\n24\t+    \"\"\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — {1}{W}{W} — 3/3.\n25\t \n26\t-    pass\n27\t+    Creature — Cat Cleric\n28\t+\n29\t+    When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and\n30\t+    black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls\n31\t+    more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\n32\t+\n33\t+    Prepare spell: Swords to Plowshares — {W} — Instant\n34\t+    Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\n35\t+\n36\t+    SOS collector number 13.\n37\t+    \"\"\"\n38\t+\n39\t+    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n40\t+        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\")\n41\t+        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\"))\n42\t+        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Cat\", \"Cleric\"})\n43\t+        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 3)\n44\t+        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 3)\n45\t+        kwargs.setdefault(\n46\t+            \"rules_text\",\n47\t+            \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white \"\n48\t+            \"and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an \"\n49\t+            \"opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature \"\n50\t+            \"becomes prepared.\",\n51\t+        )\n52\t+        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n53\t+        self.is_prepared: bool = False\n54\t+\n55\t+    def get_targets(self, game: GameState) -> list[Any]:\n56\t+        \"\"\"Target player for the ETB ability.\"\"\"\n57\t+        return [\n58\t+            TargetRequirement(\n59\t+                filter_fn=lambda obj: hasattr(obj, \"life\"),\n60\t+                description=\"target player\",\n61\t+                zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n62\t+            )\n63\t+        ]\n64\t+\n65\t+    def on_resolve(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n66\t+        \"\"\"Schedule the ETB effect on the stack for after the creature enters.\n67\t+\n68\t+        The engine fires the ETB event before registering the card's own\n69\t+        triggers (by design, to avoid self-referencing), so self-ETB\n70\t+        effects must be pushed onto the stack from on_resolve.  The\n71\t+        stack object resolves after the creature has moved to the\n72\t+        battlefield, so creature counts are correct for the prepared\n73\t+        check.\n74\t+        \"\"\"\n75\t+        from engine.stack import StackObject\n76\t+\n77\t+        source = self\n78\t+\n79\t+        def _etb_callback(g: GameState) -> None:\n80\t+            _do_etb_effect(g, source)\n81\t+\n82\t+        stack_obj = StackObject(\n83\t+            source=self,\n84\t+            controller=self.controller or self.owner,\n85\t+            on_resolve=_etb_callback,\n86\t+        )\n87\t+        game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n88\t+\n89\t+    def register_triggers(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n90\t+        \"\"\"Register the ETB trigger for Inkling token creation and prepared check.\n91\t+\n92\t+        This trigger fires when the creature re-enters the battlefield\n93\t+        (e.g. after being flickered).  The initial ETB on cast is handled\n94\t+        by on_resolve pushing a stack object.\n95\t+        \"\"\"\n96\t+        from engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n97\t+\n98\t+        source = self\n99\t+        controller = getattr(self, \"controller\", None) or game.active_player\n100\t+\n101\t+        def _condition(game: Any, event: EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent) -> bool:\n102\t+            \"\"\"Only fire when this creature itself enters the battlefield.\"\"\"\n103\t+            return event.permanent is source\n104\t+\n105\t+        def _effect(game: GameState) -> None:\n106\t+            _do_etb_effect(game, source)\n107\t+\n108\t+        game.trigger_manager.register(\n109\t+            TriggerRegistration(\n110\t+                event_type=EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent,\n111\t+                condition=_condition,\n112\t+                effect=_effect,\n113\t+                source=self,\n114\t+                controller=controller,\n115\t+            )\n116\t+        )\n117\t+\n118\t+\n119\t+def _do_etb_effect(game: Any, source: EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares) -> None:\n120\t+    \"\"\"Execute the ETB effect: create Inkling token, then check prepared.\n121\t+\n122\t+    Creates a 1/1 white+black Inkling creature token with flying for the\n123\t+    target player, then sets is_prepared if an opponent controls more\n124\t+    creatures than the controller.\n125\t+    \"\"\"\n126\t+    from engine.game import create_token\n127\t+\n128\t+    ctrl = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n129\t+    if ctrl is None:\n130\t+        return\n131\t+\n132\t+    # Determine the target player from chosen_targets.\n133\t+    chosen = getattr(source, \"chosen_targets\", None)\n134\t+    target_player = chosen[0] if chosen else ctrl\n135\t+\n136\t+    # Create a 1/1 white+black Inkling creature token with flying.\n137\t+    inkling = Creature(\n138\t+        name=\"Inkling\",\n139\t+        base_power=1,\n140\t+        base_toughness=1,\n141\t+        subtypes={\"Inkling\"},\n142\t+        keywords=Keyword.FLYING,\n143\t+        owner=target_player,\n144\t+        controller=target_player,\n145\t+    )\n146\t+    inkling.is_token = True\n147\t+    create_token(game, target_player, inkling)\n148\t+\n149\t+    # Check prepared condition: if any opponent controls more creatures\n150\t+    # than the controller.\n151\t+    ctrl_creatures = _count_creatures(game, ctrl)\n152\t+    for player in game.players:\n153\t+        if player is ctrl:\n154\t+            continue\n155\t+        opp_creatures = _count_creatures(game, player)\n156\t+        if opp_creatures > ctrl_creatures:\n157\t+            source.is_prepared = True\n158\t+            break\n159\t+\n160\t+\n161\t+def _count_creatures(game: Any, player: Any) -> int:\n162\t+    \"\"\"Count the number of creatures on a player's battlefield.\"\"\"\n163\t+    bf = game.get_battlefield(player)\n164\t+    count = 0\n165\t+    for obj in bf.get_all():\n166\t+        card_types = getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n167\t+        if CardType.CREATURE in card_types:\n168\t+            count += 1\n169\t+    return count\n170\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ChGr58yCcpZRkviDx6c1ub","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"4671f981-3b0c-44cd-b3a1-fb71712fdbb7","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:13:40.034Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend tests for sos_13 prepared mechanic"}
