{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WBr3ZY68FuZsZSWeMbKRF4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale: SOS 57 — Mana Sculpt\n2\t\n3\t## File: cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py\n4\t\n5\t### TestManaSculptProperties (4 tests)\n6\tValidates static card data matches the card spec:\n7\t- **test_is_instant**: Mana Sculpt must be an Instant subclass.\n8\t- **test_name**: Name must be \"Mana Sculpt\".\n9\t- **test_mana_cost**: Mana cost must parse to {1}{U}{U}.\n10\t- **test_card_type_includes_instant**: card_types must include CardType.INSTANT.\n11\t\n12\t### TestManaSculptTargeting (4 tests)\n13\tValidates the targeting mechanism:\n14\t- **test_returns_target_requirement_when_spell_on_stack**: get_targets() should return a TargetRequirement when there's a spell on the stack.\n15\t- **test_target_zone_is_stack**: The target requirement's zone should be Zone.STACK.\n16\t- **test_cannot_cast_with_empty_stack**: can_cast() should return False when the stack is empty (nothing to counter).\n17\t- **test_can_cast_with_spell_on_stack**: can_cast() should return True when there's a spell on the stack.\n18\t\n19\t### TestManaSculptCounterEffect (3 tests)\n20\tValidates the core counter effect:\n21\t- **test_countered_spell_goes_to_graveyard**: The countered spell's card ends up in its owner's graveyard.\n22\t- **test_countered_spell_removed_from_stack**: The StackObject is removed from the game stack.\n23\t- **test_no_target_is_a_noop**: If chosen_targets is empty/unset, on_resolve should not raise.\n24\t\n25\t### TestManaSculptWizardCheck (2 tests)\n26\tValidates the Wizard condition:\n27\t- **test_no_wizard_no_mana_added**: Without a Wizard on the battlefield, no mana is added even after advancing to the next main phase.\n28\t- **test_with_wizard_triggers_mana_production**: With a Wizard controlled, resolution should set up a delayed trigger or mechanism for mana production.\n29\t\n30\t### TestManaSculptDelayedMana (3 tests)\n31\tValidates the delayed mana production:\n32\t- **test_mana_amount_equals_countered_spell_cmc**: Countering a CMC-5 spell should produce 5 colorless mana at the next main phase.\n33\t- **test_mana_amount_for_cheap_spell**: Countering a CMC-1 spell should produce 1 colorless mana.\n34\t- **test_mana_is_colorless**: Only colorless mana (ManaType.COLORLESS) should be added, not any colored mana.\n35\t\n36\t### TestManaSculptEdgeCases (4 tests)\n37\tEdge cases and interactions:\n38\t- **test_wizard_leaves_before_resolve_no_mana**: If the Wizard leaves the battlefield before Mana Sculpt resolves, no delayed trigger is created (Wizard check happens at resolution time).\n39\t- **test_spell_still_countered_even_without_wizard**: The counter effect is unconditional — the Wizard condition only gates the mana bonus.\n40\t- **test_counter_creature_spell**: Mana Sculpt targets \"target spell\" (any spell), including creature spells.\n41\t- **test_zero_cost_spell_yields_zero_mana**: A zero-cost spell produces zero colorless mana (edge case for the amount calculation).\n42\t\n43\t## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n44\t\n45\t- **X-cost spells**: The oracle text says \"mana spent to cast that spell\". For X-cost spells, the actual mana spent differs from CMC. This is an ambiguity in how the engine tracks \"mana spent\" vs \"mana value\". The engine currently records `colors_spent` but not a total mana spent amount. This is noted in untestable.json.\n46\t- **Multiple Wizards**: Having multiple Wizards should not double the mana — the condition is \"if you control a Wizard\" (binary check). This is implicitly covered by the existing tests.\n47\t- **Delayed trigger timing with \"your next main phase\"**: The exact timing semantics (precombat vs postcombat, whose turn) are tested implicitly via the main phase advancement.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WLvMmWfkcWxuQCVULimEL7","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"81d2716c-23aa-4c49-a4a6-b6472fc1973c","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:27:46.946Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57"}
