{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01L6ygzdKJjRiZghrvVpgmsV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ATv1FcsR7YhC1FGJiHmFE4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 156,\n    \"comment\": \"The TriggerRegistration uses event_type=TriggeredEvent with condition=None, meaning it will fire on ANY TriggeredEvent in the game (ETB triggers, death triggers, etc.), not just 'beginning of your next main phase.' Combined with the StackObject also pushed at line 167, this creates a double-counting risk: the mana effect runs once from the StackObject resolving and again every time any TriggeredEvent fires. While the tests pass because they never fire events, this is a correctness bug relative to the Oracle text. The trigger should either (a) have a condition that checks for the correct phase/player, or (b) the TriggerRegistration should be removed entirely since the StackObject alone satisfies the test requirements.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 141,\n    \"comment\": \"The 'if cmc <= 0: pass' block is dead code — it does nothing and falls through to the same code that runs when cmc > 0. The comment says 'still register a trigger for consistency' but that happens regardless of this block. Consider removing the dead branch for clarity.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 109,\n    \"comment\": \"The filter_fn lambda captures 'self' but compares 'obj is not self'. Since filter_fn receives StackObjects (not card instances), 'obj is not self' will always be True because self is a Card. This is harmless and consistent with the fdn_48 Refute reference implementation, but worth noting that the filter doesn't actu