{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqcfCwp7UhDWafGt6pYGSz","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/game_state.py:76:        # Complex interactions ('skip your next turn', multiple extra turns\nengine/game_state.py:78:        self.extra_turns: list[int] = []\nengine/game_state.py:150:            if self.extra_turns:\nengine/game_state.py:155:                self.active_player_index = self.extra_turns.pop(0)\nengine/turn.py:49:    turn 1) skips their draw step on that first turn.  This is per\nengine/turn.py:52:    # The starting player skips their draw on turn 1.\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:16:| `game_state.py` | 180+ | `GameState` — central state container holding players, stack, trigger/effect/replacement managers, combat state, phase/step tracking, turn number, priority index. `extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO queue for extra turn management. `_normal_next_index` for tracking normal rotation independently. `_TURN_SEQUENCE` constant. `advance_phase()` for turn progression (pops extra turns without advancing normal rotation). |\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:26:| `turn.py` | 181 | `run_turn()` — full turn loop. Turn-based actions: untap step, draw step (skip turn 1 for starting player), combat delegation, cleanup (discard to hand size, clear damage/effects/mana, re-cleanup loop). |\nengine/DIRECTORY_SUMMARY.md:31:- **`GameState`** — The central authority; passed to nearly every function. Now includes `extra_turns` queue."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01YTug4FjT75hgzoXKoKn9cv","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"a2620c99-c853-461f-903e-f5d2454e1fc0","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:33:38.456Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_97"}
