{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MESh7GQdAfQpSCeSzGz9Bg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TZRRthMsbp726j6NhBGgqt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: sos_97 -- Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Planeswalker Structure\n- Extended the `Planeswalker` base class following the same pattern used by FDN planeswalkers (Vivien Reid, Chandra Flameshaper, Ajani).\n- Constructor uses `kwargs.setdefault()` pattern and sets Legendary supertype and \"Ral\" subtype.\n- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility` instances with correct loyalty costs (+1, -1, -2, -7).\n\n### +1: Surveil 2\n- Looks at top N cards (min of 2 and library size), then uses `controller.choose_card()` in a loop to let the player select cards to put into graveyard.\n- Each scripted choice that matches a card in the top set is moved to graveyard; others stay on top.\n- Gracefully handles libraries with fewer than 2 cards.\n\n### -1: Discard\n- Iterates over `chosen_targets` (player list), and for each targeted player with cards in hand, calls `player.choose_card()` to select a discard.\n- Handles empty hands and empty target lists gracefully.\n\n### -2: Reanimate\n- Moves target creature from whatever graveyard contains it to the controller's battlefield.\n- `get_targets()` returns a `TargetRequirement` with a filter for creatures with MV <= 3 in the graveyard zone.\n\n### -7: Coin Flip Ultimate\n- Uses `random.randint(0, 1)` for each of 5 coin flips (1 = heads).\n- Sets `opponent.skip_turns` attribute to the heads count.\n- The test monkey-patches `random.randint` to control outcomes -- this pattern works cleanly.\n\n### No Engine Modifications\n- No engine changes were needed. The card uses only existing Planeswalker, LoyaltyAbility, TargetRequirement, and zone APIs.\n- The `skip_turns` attribute is dynamically set on the player object (Python allows this), which is sufficient for the test contract.\n\n## Conventions\n- Coin flips use `random.randint(0, 1)` where 1 = heads -- tests can monkey-patch this.\n- Turn-skipping is tracked via `player.skip_turns` attribute (additive).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87,"cache_read_input_tokens":62338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":87,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019NH15HbfnxSs1UumsdQhpQ","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"aec72a5a-0cbd-4594-ae4e-7d4e9892ee2f","request_id":"req_011CbUuKa6ULEUK9JVkaGHwJ","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97"}
