{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUXCmVGuLZC9pizkFfLXqe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_97 -- Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Planeswalker Structure\n6\t- Extended the `Planeswalker` base class following the same pattern used by FDN planeswalkers (Vivien Reid, Chandra Flameshaper, Ajani).\n7\t- Constructor uses `kwargs.setdefault()` pattern and sets Legendary supertype and \"Ral\" subtype.\n8\t- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility` instances with correct loyalty costs (+1, -1, -2, -7).\n9\t\n10\t### +1: Surveil 2\n11\t- Looks at top N cards (min of 2 and library size), then uses `controller.choose_card()` in a loop to let the player select cards to put into graveyard.\n12\t- Each scripted choice that matches a card in the top set is moved to graveyard; others stay on top.\n13\t- Gracefully handles libraries with fewer than 2 cards.\n14\t\n15\t### -1: Discard\n16\t- Iterates over `chosen_targets` (player list), and for each targeted player with cards in hand, calls `player.choose_card()` to select a discard.\n17\t- Handles empty hands and empty target lists gracefully.\n18\t\n19\t### -2: Reanimate\n20\t- Moves target creature from whatever graveyard contains it to the controller's battlefield.\n21\t- `get_targets()` returns a `TargetRequirement` with a filter for creatures with MV <= 3 in the graveyard zone.\n22\t\n23\t### -7: Coin Flip Ultimate\n24\t- Uses `random.randint(0, 1)` for each of 5 coin flips (1 = heads).\n25\t- Sets `opponent.skip_turns` attribute to the heads count.\n26\t- The test monkey-patches `random.randint` to control outcomes -- this pattern works cleanly.\n27\t\n28\t### No Engine Modifications\n29\t- No engine changes were needed. The card uses only existing Planeswalker, LoyaltyAbility, TargetRequirement, and zone APIs.\n30\t- The `skip_turns` attribute is dynamically set on the player object (Python allows this), which is sufficient for the test contract.\n31\t\n32\t## Conventions\n33\t- Coin flips use `random.randint(0, 1)` where 1 = heads -- tests can monkey-patch this.\n34\t- Turn-skipping is tracked via `player.skip_turns` attribute (additive).\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FDMEtpQ3ZvLTtxxDBywmQp","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"fadd962d-6cc4-4ae8-a97b-a057f8ad9a6d","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:40:47.493Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
