{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJCSXt2zANLVHpZ4nwMt7H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent decision log across all runs.\n4\t\n5\t## sos_1: Exile replacement via marker flag\n6\t- For cards that exile spells cast from graveyard (\"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"), a `_<source>_exile` marker attribute on the card is checked in `engine/casting.py`'s `_resolve_spell()`.\n7\t- This avoids deeper engine restructuring (the ReplacementManager handles battlefield-leaving replacements, not stack-to-graveyard).\n8\t\n9\t## sos_1: Cost reduction pattern\n10\t- `cost_reduction(game)` returns the raw count (unclamped). The engine's `get_cost_reduction()` handles clamping at generic cost.\n11\t\n12\t## sos_4: Converge mechanic pattern\n13\t- Converge cards use a `colors_spent` list attribute on the card object. X = `len(set(colors_spent))` for distinct colors.\n14\t- The casting system or tests set `colors_spent` directly on the card.\n15\t\n16\t## sos_13: Prepared designation pattern\n17\t- Cards with \"prepare\" use `is_prepared` attribute on the creature.\n18\t- The `resolve_prepare_spell(game, target)` method pattern implements the prepare spell effect.\n19\t- Record creature stats (power, controller) before zone moves to ensure consistency.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FDMEtpQ3ZvLTtxxDBywmQp","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"a7d59460-611b-450e-9bc7-0f61d67bf941","timestamp":"2026-05-28T11:40:58.702Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
