{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013y23F1N3CRQyvoLP6TK2vo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DuYq6Dm9vZNsx68jpQDUPF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 154,\n    \"comment\": \"The Paradigm delayed trigger effect (_paradigm_effect) is a no-op (`pass`). The oracle text says 'you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.' This core functionality is entirely unimplemented. The trigger fires but does nothing. This is a significant spec violation -- the recurring free-cast from exile is a key part of the Paradigm keyword.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 120,\n    \"comment\": \"Double zone-move conflict: on_resolve sets `_paradigm_exile = True` (line 120) AND directly moves self from stack to exile (lines 130-132). When called through the full casting pipeline (_resolve_spell in engine/casting.py), _resolve_spell will then try move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE) but the card was already removed from the stack by on_resolve. move_to_zone silently returns (safety check at line 255 of zones.py), so no crash, but the intent is redundant and fragile. The direct move bypasses move_to_zone hooks. Choose ONE approach: either set the marker flag and let _resolve_spell handle the zone move, OR do the move directly in on_resolve and do not set the flag. The flag approach is consistent with the _dawning_archaic_exile pattern from sos_1, so the direct move (lines 122-132) should be removed.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 100,\n    \"comment\": \"The free-cast implementation calls card.on_resolve(game) directly rather than going through the casting pipeline (cast_spell or similar). This means triggers like SpellCastTriggeredEvent are never fired for the free-cast spells, ETB handling via move_to_zone is bypassed, and the permanent placement at lines 138-139 uses raw zone.add() instead of move_to_zone. This is a simplified approach that may cause issues if other cards care about cast triggers or ETB events from these free-cast spells. Acceptable as a simplification for now, but worth noting.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 136,\n    \"comment\": \"game._paradigm_registered is a monkey-patched set on the game state. If the game state is ever copied or reset, this tracking will be lost. Also, this is per card-name but not per player -- if two different players both resolve Improvisation Capstone, only the first player's Paradigm trigger gets registered. The oracle text says 'After you first resolve a spell with this name' which is per-player, not global.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1113,"cache_read_input_tokens":36165,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1113,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AdrYPRBDk5FiWYHm9Vqurq","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"afb9c441-43ca-44fa-96f0-69a2f0bddac4","request_id":"req_011CbUvKEuRmnWuc7fBwwG1E","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
