{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CiKb7vR4XMuueansAJ6QfV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UJoCpFUaaro9ojAXAWvAVi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale for sos_226 -- Silverquill, the Disputant\n\n## File: cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py\n\n### TestSilverquillProperties (8 tests)\nValidates all static card properties against the card spec:\n\n- **test_is_creature**: Silverquill must be a Creature subclass.\n- **test_name**: Card name must be \"Silverquill, the Disputant\".\n- **test_mana_cost**: Mana cost must be {2}{W}{B}.\n- **test_power_toughness**: base_power and base_toughness must be 4.\n- **test_has_flying**: Keywords must include FLYING.\n- **test_has_vigilance**: Keywords must include VIGILANCE.\n- **test_is_legendary**: Supertypes must include LEGENDARY.\n- **test_subtypes_include_elder_and_dragon**: Subtypes must include \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\".\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyRegistration (3 tests)\nValidates that Silverquill registers trigger(s) for the casualty-granting ability when it enters the battlefield:\n\n- **test_registers_trigger_on_battlefield**: register_triggers must add at least one trigger.\n- **test_registered_trigger_watches_spell_cast_event**: The trigger must watch for SpellCastTriggeredEvent (since casualty triggers when you cast an instant or sorcery).\n- **test_trigger_source_is_silverquill**: The trigger's source must be the Silverquill card itself (for proper unregistration when it leaves).\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyCondition (4 tests)\nValidates the trigger condition: casualty 1 applies only to instants and sorceries cast by the controller, not creatures or opponent spells:\n\n- **test_trigger_fires_for_instant_spell_by_controller**: An instant cast by the controller matches the condition.\n- **test_trigger_fires_for_sorcery_spell_by_controller**: A sorcery cast by the controller matches the condition.\n- **test_trigger_does_not_fire_for_creature_spell**: A creature spell does NOT match (casualty only applies to instants/sorceries).\n- **test_trigger_does_not_fire_for_opponent_spell**: An opponent's instant does NOT match (casualty is only for \"spells you cast\").\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyEffect (2 tests)\nValidates the casualty copy mechanic:\n\n- **test_casualty_paid_creates_copy_on_stack**: When casualty is paid (sacrifice marker set), the trigger fires and something is pushed on the stack (the copy or the copy trigger).\n- **test_no_sacrifice_no_copy**: When casualty is NOT paid, no copy is created. Also verifies the trigger is registered (preventing vacuous pass from stub).\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyPowerThreshold (3 tests)\nValidates the power requirement for casualty 1:\n\n- **test_creature_with_power_zero_cannot_pay_casualty**: A creature with power 0 cannot satisfy casualty 1.\n- **test_creature_with_power_one_can_pay_casualty**: A creature with power exactly 1 can satisfy casualty 1.\n- **test_creature_with_power_greater_than_one_can_pay_casualty**: A creature with power > 1 can satisfy casualty 1.\n\nThese tests use a flexible approach: they check for a `can_pay_casualty` method if present, or fall back to verifying `casualty_n == 1` to confirm the threshold is correctly stored.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtySacrifice (1 test)\nValidates that the sacrificed creature is removed from the battlefield:\n\n- **test_sacrificed_creature_leaves_battlefield**: After casualty payment, the sacrificed creature should no longer be on the battlefield.\n\n### TestSilverquillLeavesPlay (1 test)\nValidates cleanup when Silverquill leaves:\n\n- **test_triggers_unregistered_on_leave**: When the trigger manager unregisters Silverquill, its triggers are removed so subsequent casts do not get casualty.\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Opponent's spells do not get casualty (controller-only check)\n- Creature spells do not get casualty (instant/sorcery-only check)\n- Power 0 creature cannot pay casualty 1\n- When casualty is not paid, no copy is created\n- Trigger cleanup on leave\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (out of scope)\n- Multiple Silverquills granting multiple instances of casualty (702.153b handles this but is a complex interaction beyond single-card scope)\n- Choosing new targets for the copy (depends on full casting pipeline target-selection infrastructure)\n- Interaction with counterspells (engine-level behavior)\n- Casualty with X spells or spells with additional costs (not specific to this card)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":67563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1158,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LSwiN9oWp7CG9ixhukbp27","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"7d539308-11df-473a-a61b-1bdb6eb96916","request_id":"req_011CbUwVtku4CxtVtu3rABja","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_226"}
