{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Tecxo6kWUWeDCVtrgKkWrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TV5WugyVntVCa9Koi985Ph","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale: sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Creature subclass with static properties\nSilverquill is implemented as a `Creature` subclass following the established pattern from sos_201 (Lorehold). The constructor sets name, mana cost, power/toughness, supertypes (Legendary), subtypes (Elder, Dragon), and keywords (Flying, Vigilance) via kwargs defaults.\n\n### Casualty as a triggered ability\nCasualty 1 is implemented as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger registered via `register_triggers()`. This follows the same pattern used by Lorehold for its spell-watching triggers.\n\n**Condition**: Checks that the spell is an instant or sorcery AND that the caster is the controller of Silverquill. This allows the trigger to fire for all qualifying spells -- the casualty payment check is deferred to the effect.\n\n**Effect**: Checks `spell._casualty_paid` flag. If True, the sacrificed creature (`spell._casualty_sacrificed`) is moved from the battlefield to the graveyard, and `copy_spell()` is used to create a copy on the stack. If False, the effect is a no-op.\n\n### Casualty validation helper\n`can_pay_casualty(game, creature)` is a method on the card that checks if a creature's power >= `casualty_n` (class attribute set to 1). This provides a clean API for the game engine or UI to validate casualty targets.\n\n### Casualty payment protocol\nThe implementation uses a marker-flag protocol (`_casualty_paid`, `_casualty_sacrificed`) on the spell card object, consistent with the project's established pattern (see sos_1's `_dawning_archaic_exile` marker). The casting system or tests set these flags before firing the SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n\n## Conventions Established\n- Casualty payment uses `_casualty_paid` (bool) and `_casualty_sacrificed` (creature reference) marker attributes on the spell.\n- `casualty_n` class attribute defines the power threshold for the casualty cost.\n- `can_pay_casualty(game, creature)` validates individual creatures against the threshold.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87,"cache_read_input_tokens":55928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":87,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":45,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GGk6uFNdhHSGftNKL6bdAX","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"a6d2aaf1-3203-4235-9f93-f141ddfc055d","request_id":"req_011CbUwh4FTREWbvSSNEE7UC","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
