{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZRLCXK5o1VH6nDVbkdpq8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Creature subclass with static properties\n6\tSilverquill is implemented as a `Creature` subclass following the established pattern from sos_201 (Lorehold). The constructor sets name, mana cost, power/toughness, supertypes (Legendary), subtypes (Elder, Dragon), and keywords (Flying, Vigilance) via kwargs defaults.\n7\t\n8\t### Casualty as a triggered ability\n9\tCasualty 1 is implemented as a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger registered via `register_triggers()`. This follows the same pattern used by Lorehold for its spell-watching triggers.\n10\t\n11\t**Condition**: Checks that the spell is an instant or sorcery AND that the caster is the controller of Silverquill. This allows the trigger to fire for all qualifying spells -- the casualty payment check is deferred to the effect.\n12\t\n13\t**Effect**: Checks `spell._casualty_paid` flag. If True, the sacrificed creature (`spell._casualty_sacrificed`) is moved from the battlefield to the graveyard, and `copy_spell()` is used to create a copy on the stack. If False, the effect is a no-op.\n14\t\n15\t### Casualty validation helper\n16\t`can_pay_casualty(game, creature)` is a method on the card that checks if a creature's power >= `casualty_n` (class attribute set to 1). This provides a clean API for the game engine or UI to validate casualty targets.\n17\t\n18\t### Casualty payment protocol\n19\tThe implementation uses a marker-flag protocol (`_casualty_paid`, `_casualty_sacrificed`) on the spell card object, consistent with the project's established pattern (see sos_1's `_dawning_archaic_exile` marker). The casting system or tests set these flags before firing the SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n20\t\n21\t## Conventions Established\n22\t- Casualty payment uses `_casualty_paid` (bool) and `_casualty_sacrificed` (creature reference) marker attributes on the spell.\n23\t- `casualty_n` class attribute defines the power threshold for the casualty cost.\n24\t- `can_pay_casualty(game, creature)` validates individual creatures against the threshold.\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TwqPusYe4y3G6gErn3GwYb","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"a88da554-33d9-40fa-ad03-bedfdeeb288e","timestamp":"2026-05-28T12:11:51.660Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_226 implementation"}
