{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UqozjT2DAeakTynywYQitL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Land subclass with dynamic creature properties\n6\t- Extends `Land` (not `Creature`) since it starts as a land. When animated, `CardType.CREATURE` is added to `card_types` and `power`/`toughness` are exposed via properties.\n7\t- Used `@property` for `power`, `toughness`, `base_power`, `base_toughness` that return values only when `_is_animated` is True, matching the test expectations that check both property names.\n8\t\n9\t### Mana abilities with closure-based cost functions\n10\t- Cost functions use single-arg `(game)` signature with the card captured via closure (`source = self`). This matches how tests call `ability.cost(game)` directly without needing the two-arg fallback.\n11\t- Follows the `fdn_267` Secluded Courtyard pattern but simplified to single-arg closures.\n12\t\n13\t### Any-color mana ability with life payment\n14\t- The tap + pay 1 life cost is handled atomically in the cost function: checks not tapped, checks life >= 1, then taps and deducts life.\n15\t- ENGINE LIMITATION: Spending restriction (\"only to cast instant or sorcery\") is not enforced per engine limitations, same as Secluded Courtyard's approach.\n16\t\n17\t### Animation via activated ability\n18\t- The `{5}` cost uses `ManaCost(generic=5)` with `can_pay`/`pay` on the controller's mana pool.\n19\t- The effect checks \"if this land isn't a creature\" before animating, matching the card's conditional.\n20\t- On animation, adds `CardType.CREATURE` and `\"Wizard\"` subtype, sets `_is_animated = True`.\n21\t\n22\t### Triggered ability registration on animation\n23\t- A `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger is registered when the land is animated.\n24\t- Condition checks: controller matches, and spell has INSTANT or SORCERY card type.\n25\t- Effect increments `_power_bonus` which is added to the base power of 2 in the `power` property.\n26\t- Pump stacks across multiple casts as tested by `test_multiple_instants_stack_pump`.\n27\t\n28\t## Deviations\n29\t- None. Implementation follows card spec directly.\n30\t\n31\t## Conventions\n32\t- For lands that animate into creatures, use `@property` for power/toughness instead of inheriting from Creature, since the card starts as a non-creature permanent.\n33\t- Capture `self` as `source` in closures for mana/activated ability callbacks.\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01C2BAF6ShCuGXBYCTxncvgX","session_id":"61c1c383-66ff-4b43-bc55-e6e3182b632f","uuid":"33f2fb3f-b0e3-4d5f-898f-90c632107de4","timestamp":"2026-05-28T12:34:54.334Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
